|* ro_stage noise mechanism check -- self-biased inverting amplifier
|*
|* Purpose: confirm ngspice's .noise analysis produces a non-zero,
|* non-NaN, non-flat output noise spectrum for design/xschem/ro_stage.sch's
|* starved-inverter delay cell (sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 / __pfet_01v8), i.e.
|* that the flicker-noise mechanism DR-0001 depends on
|* (noia/noib/noic -- kf/af are present in the model card but zeroed and
|* therefore inert, see DR-0001 Consequences and issue #9's own "Verified
|* corrections") is actually active in the corner decks as installed. This
|* is a go/no-go mechanism check, NOT the jitter-accumulation
|* characterization campaign (per-stage noise/gain, ring jitter
|* accumulation, array sizing) -- that is separate, later scope.
|*
|* ro_stage has no static operating point of its own once wired into a
|* free-running ring (an oscillator has no small-signal DC bias point in
|* the sense .noise requires), so this deck instead self-biases a single
|* ro_stage instance as an inverting small-signal amplifier around its own
|* trip voltage: a large feedback resistor (Rfb) from output back to input
|* holds the input near Vtrip with ~0 DC current, and a large series
|* resistor (Rin) couples the AC/noise reference source in without
|* disturbing that bias. This is the standard "self-biased inverter as a
|* noise amplifier" construction used to characterize CMOS inverter/ring
|* delay-cell noise ahead of a full transient jitter run.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes the
|* /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice (absolute path to the pinned sky130 ngspice corner library),
|* ss (process corner name) and /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-9/design/ro_ring5.spice (absolute path to the
|* committed, netlist.py --check-guarded design/ro_ring5.spice, which
|* defines the ro_stage subcircuit this deck instantiates) placeholders
|* before invoking ngspice -- as committed here, it is not a runnable deck.
|* /var/folders/0h/l9gwswj97wb82mh27zyw305r0000gn/T/sim-corner-run-20260825-022446-d58d709-ar6mhukw/ss.onoise.txt is substituted with the path corner-run.py wants the raw
|* onoise_spectrum written to (via wrdata), for its own non-flat check.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
|
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-9/design/ro_ring5.spice"
|
|Vdd vdd 0 dc 1.8
|Vin n_in 0 dc 0 ac 1
|Rin n_in a 1e9
|Rfb y a 1e9
|
|xdut a y vdd 0 ro_stage
|
|.control
|op
|print v(a) v(y)
|noise v(y) vin dec 10 10 1g
|print onoise_total
|setplot noise1
|wrdata /var/folders/0h/l9gwswj97wb82mh27zyw305r0000gn/T/sim-corner-run-20260825-022446-d58d709-ar6mhukw/ss.onoise.txt onoise_spectrum
|.endc
|.end
|

